==Strategy==
The main threats here are the 6 Chickful As. Thankfully they don't spawn all at once, and instead in 2 groups of 3, so killing them before they stack up should be the priority. Depending on your units, you could either treat Dagshund as a stepping stone to hit them, or just as a wall to be destroyed.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - Ramen Cat is a given on any Angel-focused stage. They have high defense, and can shrug off a lot of hits. Recharge Combos make them much more efficient.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]/[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] - Both are anti-Angel attackers, but Mushroom Cat has Area Attack and higher range, while Cafeteria Cat has Curse, higher damage and shorter recharge in exchange for shorter range and Single Attack.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - At level 54 (or 45 with full Attack Talent), Can Can can kill the Gabriels in one hit, and earn a good bit of cash if the Double Bounty Talent is also used.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] - Especially useful in higher Crowns, where everything deals high damage. Can shrug off the attacks from the Chickful As with ease, though beware of the peons and Dagshunds.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any Ubers able to outrange Chickful A (371 range or higher) are quite useful, especially anti-Angel specialists such as units from the Ultra Souls banner.

